\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  When the Lord gives a partner, fit,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 With whom thou art in mutual love,
\par A precious gift you've really had
\par And you have cause for happiness.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.   A loyal bride cherish her groom,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Treats him fairly and gives him help
\par In both good times and adverse times,
\par In prosperity and in need.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  A good counsel she gives her groom,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 In adverse times she does console.
\par While in his fold she gives pleasure,
\par  It is not fit to live alone.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  Husband, thou should support thy wife!
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0   Wife, do give thy husband support,
\par  God has united thee from hence,
\par  Let none cause thee to be divorced.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.   The eyes of God keep thee in watch,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Blessed has thine unity been,
\par Mercy and grace are all we wish,
\par   To keep on course thine unity.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Thou art to watch the Lord always,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Stick to thine selves in honesty,
\par  That thou may stay in perfect peace,
\par  And so arrive in perfect bliss.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. O Lord Jesus, our Saviour dear,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj  Thou who has, by Thy precious blood,
\par Saved us from our iniquities,
\par  And brought us to Thy glorious home
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. Thy church, continue to protect,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  That married couples and the child,
\par  May so traverse Thy pious ways,
\par  And let them to Thy he'ven above.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

